WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:05.869
In the lab, you run each check against a
fictional tenant with the from-json option,

3
00:00:05.869 --> 00:00:09.975
which evaluates a saved Graph
response instead of calling Graph.

4
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:11.916
Here's step three: the PIM report,

5
00:00:11.916 --> 00:00:15.125
with the Privileged Role
Administrator role added.

6
00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:17.862
Global Administrator is always included.

7
00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:20.853
The fixture has three
Global Administrators,

8
00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:24.788
which is within two to eight, so
policy seven point one passes.

9
00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:28.548
But two principals hold
privileged roles permanently,

10
00:00:28.548 --> 00:00:32.063
with no expiration, so policy
seven point four fails.

11
00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:37.261
The PowerShell function returns exactly
the same JSON, and the Pester tests compare

12
00:00:37.261 --> 00:00:41.737
every PowerShell check with the Python
results, so the two can't drift apart.

13
00:00:41.737 --> 00:00:44.380
The lab runs all five checks this way.
